<DocsLayout title="Advanced Google ADK guide | Agent-Gantry" description="Tool confirmation, how per-turn selection works inside a run, tracing and error modes for the Agent-Gantry Google ADK integration.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Advanced framework guide</p>
  <h1>Advanced Google ADK</h1>
  <p class="lead">Tool confirmation, how per-turn selection works inside a run, and tracing.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/Agent-Gantry/docs/frameworks/google-adk/">← Basic Google ADK usage</a></p>

  <h2>Tool confirmation</h2>
  <p>A tool registered with <code>requires_confirmation=True</code>, or matched by a <code>SecurityPolicy(require_confirmation=[...])</code> pattern, sets ADK's <code>require_confirmation</code>. The run emits an <code>adk_request_confirmation</code> function call; answer it with a function response to continue.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`pending = None
async for event in runner.run_async(user_id=uid, session_id=sid, new_message=message):
    for part in (event.content.parts if event.content else None) or []:
        if part.function_call and part.function_call.name == "adk_request_confirmation":
            pending = part.function_call

if pending is not None:
    reply = types.FunctionResponse(
        name="adk_request_confirmation", id=pending.id,
        response={"confirmed": ask_a_human(pending.args["originalFunctionCall"])},
    )
    message = types.Content(role="user", parts=[types.Part(function_response=reply)])
    async for event in runner.run_async(user_id=uid, session_id=sid, new_message=message):
        ...`} />
  <p>A confirmed call runs once through <code>gantry.execute</code> with only the confirmation gate cleared; ADK refuses a rejected one itself. <code>gantry.requires_confirmation(tool)</code> answers the same question without running anything.</p>
  <p>ADK resumes a confirmed call through the agent's own tools. <code>adapter.agent()</code> includes a toolset that supplies the gated Gantry tools only on the turn answering a confirmation; if you wire <code>before_model_callback()</code> into your own agent, add <code>tools=[adapter.confirmation_toolset()]</code>.</p>

  <h2>Per-turn selection inside a run</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mechanism:</strong> before each model request the callback selects tools and injects them with <code>LlmRequest.append_tools</code>, which also registers them so ADK can run them that turn.</li>
    <li><strong>Query:</strong> the newest user message, plus the latest successful tool result after it (first 2,000 characters). An <code>&#123;"error": ...&#125;</code> response never feeds retrieval; <code>query_from_results=False</code> keeps all tool output out.</li>
    <li><strong>State:</strong> keyed by the ADK invocation, so concurrent runs are independent.</li>
    <li><strong>Stickiness:</strong> tools offered earlier in a run stay offered, up to <code>max_offered</code> (default <code>3 * limit</code>); the current selection and pinned tools always stay. Use <code>sticky=False</code> for a strict top-k.</li>
    <li><strong>Failure:</strong> if retrieval fails, the turn keeps the run's previous tools plus the pins, and logs a warning.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Run context and tracing</h2>
  <p><code>current_tool_context()</code> returns the call's ADK <code>ToolContext</code>: session <code>state</code>, <code>user_id</code>, <code>invocation_id</code>, <code>function_call_id</code>, artifacts and memory. <code>current_tool_invocation()</code> carries the same object, with <code>deps</code> set to the session state. ADK traces with OpenTelemetry, so its active span becomes the Gantry <code>ToolCall</code>'s <code>trace_id</code> and <code>parent_span_id</code>.</p>

  <h2>Production checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Handle <code>adk_request_confirmation</code> on any agent that can reach a confirmation-gated tool.</li>
    <li>Use an <code>error_formatter</code> if handler exception messages may contain internals.</li>
    <li>Pin must-have tools with <code>required=[...]</code> or <code>always_include=[...]</code>; they stay offered even when retrieval fails.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
